### Key Findings
- FOXP2 binds CNTNAP2 intron directly and represses transcription; CNTNAP2 SNPs associate with NWR language marker (P=5×10⁻⁵)
- CNTNAP2 KO mice: reduced PV+/CR+/NPY+ interneurons in cortex/striatum/hippocampus; CUX1+ migration abnormality
- LFP abnormalities precede overt epilepsy — E/I imbalance is primary, not secondary to seizures
- mPFC: delta/theta phase-locking collapse (Lazaro 2019); oscillatory coordination failure
- OXT: reduced PVN oxytocin neurons; NAc as key circuit node for social rescue (Choe 2022)
- PNN: overexpressed in mPFC PV+ cells; ChABC rescue of social but not stereotyped behavior (Gandhi 2023)

